<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Broken Isles ~ Region Worksheet

''The severed shelf.'' Once ''the eastern shelf of the great Nexus of Mu'' — coast of the drowned
low kingdoms, half-submerged pagodas and temple gates under warm reef-strewn seas — the shelf was
''ripped away during the fall of the Necrospire'' at YOLD 5000. What remains stands as three great
islands divided by deep Astral Sea rifts, fringed with sky-islands, threaded with ancient fungal
jungles.

''Two names, and the difference matters.'' Charts read ''the Broken Isles''. The rift-coast locals
say ''the Shattered Isles'', //and keep the older grief in it//. Anyone using the chart-name in a
harbor tavern is announcing where they are from.

''Dream-mirror source:'' Japan · Nusantara (mythic Thailand, Myanmar, Malaysia, Indonesia) · New
Zealand · //Nausicaä and the Valley of the Wind//.

''Why this worksheet matters at the table:'' ''two of three player-daemon PCs come from here'', and
so does the clan that carried Ichi's armor. Lady Aki's priesthood, Kai ʻĀ's hunting ranges, and the
battlefield where the household was born all sit inside this Nexus.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-severing>>

!! The Severing ~ what YOLD 5000 did here

''Three catastrophes in one season.'' The Isles carry a compound wound that no other Nexus quite
matches:

# ''The shelf tore free.'' A continuous coastline of Mu became three islands with Astral rifts
  between them. Ground that had been contiguous for aeons stopped being reachable on foot.
# ''A war was already on it.'' A ''Neo-Thracian expeditionary force'' was fighting here — several
  factional fronts at once, supply chain at its end, as far from Neo-Thracia as an imperial soldier
  could physically stand.
# ''Then the network died.'' Web 2 failed planet-wide in a day, and both sides went dark together.
  //They did not lose a battle. They lost the continent, the network, and the war at once.//

''Which is why the local name keeps the grief.'' The severing runs 492 years back and the Isles
still name themselves after it.

''What the rifts do now:'' deep Astral Sea channels between the three isles, crossed by wave-jammer,
sky-lane, or Underdark rift-gate — never on foot. The severance is permanent geography.

''Prompts:'' which clans lost kin on the far side of a rift that opened in a night · what the Mu
mainland owes, or thinks it owes, its severed shelf · whether any stretch of old coast road still
runs to a cliff and stops.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-three-isles>>

!! The Three Isles

''The Northern Isle ~ the fungal country.'' Lowest-lying, prone to flooding, ''dominated by fungal
megaflora'' whose root networks may conceal a slow semi-sentient hivemind. ''Mycohaven'' — a
port-city partially grown from fungal architecture — seats the ''Fungal Druid Circles''. This is
Mother-Culture country: anchored Mother Spore clusters in the settled parts, and beyond them the
deep fungal jungle the locals reckon in weeks rather than miles.

''The Southeastern Isle ~ the mist.'' Perpetually swathed in fog, geothermal ley-nodes feeding a
labyrinth of waterfall canyons and hidden terraces. The ''Mist Monastery'' rings ships and flyers
through the fog channels by resonant bell. ''Seelie Fae Clans'' predominate — healing plants, fog
navigation rites, frequent alliance with Hawaiki voyagers.

''The Southwestern Isle ~ the cavern cities.'' Mountainous jungle riddled with bamboo-built cavern
cities and ''Underdark rift-gates'' that serve as trade arteries and deadly hazards both.
''Kōra Caverns'' — bamboo-scaffolded, suspended markets, the Underdark trade hub for goods moving
to Mu and Hawaiki. The ''Root-Gate Chasms'' open to Nexuses across ''both Nets'' when fed the
correct spore key.

''Above all three ~ the sky-islands.'' Rooted rock masses carrying ''insect fae clans'' — hornet,
beetle, dragonfly lineages — casting shifting shadows on the seas below. ''Hivewind Heights'' holds
the hive-complex: aerial trade, mounts, and pollen diplomacy.

''Prompts:'' which isle holds Aki's priesthood and which holds Kai's ranges · what a spore key costs
and who cuts them · which sky-island has drifted somewhere it should not have.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/powers>>

!! Powers, Hazards, Nodes

''Factions:'' ''Insect Fae Clans'' (sky-island trade, aerial mounts, pollen enchantment) ·
''Cave-City Elders'' (merchant councils over Underdark commerce and jungle resources) · ''Fungal
Druid Circles'' (guardians of the megaflora, possible intermediaries to the hivemind) · ''Seelie
Fae Clans'' (mist isle) · the ''Mycelial Hivemind'' (rumored — //a distributed consciousness in the
fungal root systems; may function as a hidden Lares network//).

''Also standing here:'' the ''Shattered Isles Kaiju-Hunter Cabals'', one of the four factions the
alpha-playtest company walks in under, and the ''Spider-Mother's Priesthoods''
([[grandmother-spider|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/concepts/grandmother-spider]]).

''Lares:'' fragmented but adaptive. Grove-Lares embedded in fungal root networks; Sky-Lares in the
insect hives; Path-Lares riding with migrating aerial mounts. ''Some nodes interface only through
mycelial dream-roots'', requiring fungal communion rites to reach — a node you must be admitted to
biologically rather than by token.

''Hazards:'' spore storms drifting from the north (dangerous to breathe, and excellent cover) ·
riftquakes collapsing or flooding Underdark tunnels · mist illusions hiding reefs, and fog-spirits
luring vessels into ''temporal pockets'' · sky-island collisions.

''Strategic weight:'' the primary bridge between the Eastern Net and the Western continental
Nexuses, linked to Hawaiki's seasonal orbital path. Rich in biomagitech — ''spore engines, fungal
composites, insect-derived enchantments''.

''Prompts:'' what the hivemind wants, if it wants · who brokers between the Circles and the hives
this season · what a temporal pocket returns you into.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-wilds>>

!! The Wilds ~ the Nausicaä register

''The fungal jungles run ancient and they run deep.'' The dream-mirror names //Nausicaä and the
Valley of the Wind// outright, and the register holds: spore-air that kills the unmasked, megaflora
older than any settlement, an ecology that reads as hostile and turns out to be doing something
else, and a small number of people who have learned to walk in it without a filter and decline to
explain how.

''What the wilds hold:'' the wreck-fields of old wars, including ''the Neo-Thracian battle-grounds
of YOLD 5000'' — a whole invasion's kit lying where the network died, blast-scarred roadside
shrines among it. This is where Lady Aki followed an Ephyra and came back with a household
([[strandbeest-shrine|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/characters/companions/strandbeest-shrine]]).

''Prompts:'' what else is still standing out there with a daemon in it · what the Circles permit to
be salvaged and what they do not · why kaiju range these islands and what the hunters have learned
not to say about it.

